docker run -> 
docker-compose up -d

docker producer side(complaining) -> 
docker exec -it kafka kafka-console-producer --topic complaint-topic --bootstrap-server localhost:9092

open new terminal and run (consumer side) -> 
docker exec -it kafka kafka-console-consumer --topic complaint-topic --from-beginning --bootstrap-server localhost:9092

docker stop -> 
docker compose down  (run in terminal 1)

check container-> 
docker ps (both kafka and zookepper works)

create topic -> 
docker exec -it kafka kafka-topics --create --topic complaint-topic --bootstrap-server localhost:9092 --partitions 1 --replication-factor 1

topic exist or not -> 
docker exec -it kafka kafka-topics --list --bootstrap-server localhost:9092

overall reset -> 
docker compose down -v


steps: 

1.start the kafka
docker compose up -d

2.check container running
docker ps

output:
kafka       Up ...
zookeeper   Up ...

3.create topic 
docker exec -it kafka kafka-topics --create --topic complaint-topic --bootstrap-server localhost:9092 --partitions 1 --replication-factor 1

4.verify topic
docker exec -it kafka kafka-topics --list --bootstrap-server localhost:9092

output: complaint-topic

5.send message(producer side)
docker exec -it kafka kafka-console-producer --topic complaint-topic --bootstrap-server localhost:9092

type: FIRST_TEST_MESSAGE
ctrl+check

6.open another terminal for checking consumer side message 
docker exec -it kafka kafka-console-consumer --topic complaint-topic --from-beginning --bootstrap-server localhost:9092

7.restart the kafka for checking previous message exist or not
docker compose down
docker compose up -d

wait : 60-90 seconds for restart

8.check for already created topic is present or not , if present kafka works correctly , we will recover the old message
if it is not present then we have to create topic again and check for message

9.if topic is present then check for message
docker exec -it kafka kafka-console-consumer --topic complaint-topic --from-beginning --bootstrap-server localhost:9092

output: FIRST_TEST_MESSAGE
